{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788977446,"nonce":"TazWs2501CbNXZRwmqLIiax/iQQ=","title":"A release build silently embeds the debug runtime when the release one is missing","message":"`crates/ash/build.rs` looks for the `ash_std` cdylib in the triple-qualified and\nplain target directories, and when the profile is not `debug` it also falls back\nto the debug ones. The fallback is legal but hides a real mismatch: a release\n`ash` emitting calls into a stale release `libash_std.dylib` looks correct\nlocally, because the embedded copy came from the debug tree that happens to be\nnewer.\n\nIt surfaces only where a separate runtime is staged beside the program, which is\nhow an unresolved `hlp_alloc_obj_sized` reached the promoter. The two artifacts\nhave no version relationship enforced anywhere.\n\nOptions, cheapest first: make the fallback loud rather than silent; or refuse it\noutright in a release build and say which command to run; or stamp both with a\nbuild id and check them at load.","files":null}]}